       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I can see the following potential options:</p>\n\n<p>1) leave it to a workflow engine to manage (the workflow engine would be responsible for persisting state)<br/>\n2) use the existing state attribute (extend the values permitted)<br/>\n3) have a new state attribute<br/>\n4) have generic methods for adding and manipulating custom object and datastream properties (repository developers can then define their own state attribute(s) as required)<br/>\n5) do it in RELS-EXT/RELS-INT</p>\n\n<p>I would tend to favour (4) as it doesn't prescribe how state should be modeled and persisted wrt workflow, but gives developers the ability to implement whatever they need.  However there does seem to be potential overlap with RELS-EXT/RELS-INT in this approach.</p>\n\n<p>Also, we currently have in FOXML optional extproperty elements to store \"custom\" properties - but no API methods to manipulate them - perhaps adding API methods for these would suffice at this stage?  (The original reporter only seems to mention tracking \"state\" at the object, rather than datastream, level)</p>",
     "created": "24/Aug/09 9:13 AM",
