      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Decided 9/1/09, need improved docs on relationship API, see \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-528\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-528\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Better Documentation/Examples on relationship API\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-528\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n.  Consensus was that workflow state management is not a central concern of the repository and we need real use cases to motivate changing Fedora's definition of STATE to go beyond (Active, Inactive, Deleted).  Possible future special topic meeting if motivated by a group doing workflow who wants to see a change to Fedora to facilitate this.</p>",
